		{
			"id": "eE1SLK9NH3apdOUbW",
			"description": "Omnissian Axe",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle and depleted-cell rules as the Imperium Power Sword.\n\nLore: A ceremonial axe carried by senior Tech-Priests as a badge of office and a functional close combat weapon in equal measure, current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background depicting it wreathed in a disruption field identical in effect to an Astartes or Militarum power weapon - the Cult Mechanicus reveres the technology behind the field as much as it uses the weapon itself.\n\nDesign: Per framework.md's own instruction that a bolter built for the Astartes armoury and one carried by a Sister of Battle are the same weapon with the same numbers, this is mechanically identical to the Imperium Power Axe (sw+3d+2(10) cut field on / sw+2 cut field off, the power-field rule established under Power Sword) rather than a re-derived Mechanicus-specific disruption field - nothing in the lore suggests a Tech-Priest's field works any differently from an Astartes officer's, only that the Cult Mechanicus treats the underlying technology as a sacred mystery rather than standard-issue wargear, which is reflected in cost and legality (LC1, Mechanicus-restricted) rather than a different damage line. The one stated difference is handling: parry 0 (a ritually counterweighted haft, so it can parry in the turn it strikes) where the Imperium Power Axe is 0U (unbalanced: it cannot, B269).",
