		{
			"id": "eQPFuNRPxjaPsi0qS",
			"description": "Power Goad",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A long-handled prod used by Tech-Priests and Magos-overseers to administer correction to servitors, indentured menials and disobedient Kataphron husks; background material treats it as a tool of discipline within the Cult Mechanicus hierarchy rather than a war weapon, closer in spirit to a cattle-prod than to a power weapon.\n\nDesign: Not built from the power-field rule at all, despite the name: framework.md's power-field rule is reserved for genuine disruption-field weapons meant to kill (the Omnissian Axe/Staff above), and nothing in the goad's lore suggests it is meant to. Instead it follows the Imperium Shock Maul/Staff family's own design (a plain thrusting weapon, thr cr, plus a Basic Set HT-roll stun effect layered on top rather than extra damage), at a milder HT-2 rather than the Shock Maul's HT-3, reflecting a tool built to correct rather than to incapacitate outright. TL11 for the internal charge cell; LC2 (Mechanicus/enforcement-tier, matching the framework's Shock Maul bracket) rather than LC1, since this is disciplinary rather than combat-restricted gear.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "900",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wYXHBgXPLcc_Sn8Ib",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "thr"
					},
					"reach": "1,2",
					"parry": "-1",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Thrust",
					"usage_notes": "A hit that does any HP of damage forces the target to roll HT-2 or be stunned (B420), as the Imperium Shock Maul's electro-stun rule at a milder setting - a goad is built to discipline and herd, not to kill.\n",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
