		{
			"id": "epVYG-ftK7Q19TRHX",
			"description": "Arc Goad",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A goad built around the same capacitor-discharge principle as an arc weapon rather than a simple electro-shock cell, used specifically to correct and discipline the Cult Mechanicus's own cybernetic servants - a rogue servitor or an under-performing Kataphron husk - by shocking its internal systems directly rather than merely hurting whatever flesh remains.\n\nDesign: Combines the Power Goad's plain thr cr baseline with the Arc Pistol's own machine-disabling surge rule rather than its raw damage line, since the whole point of this variant is correcting machines, not people: the HT-3 penalty sits at the lower end of the arc-weapon family's escalating penalties (pistol -2, rifle -4, heavy rifle -6), appropriate for a melee-range prod rather than a dedicated ranged weapon. No organic-target stun note is included, unlike the Power Goad or Taser Goad, since an arc discharge's whole design purpose in this project is to be \"weak against flesh,\" per framework.md's arc-weapon anchor.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "1400",
			"base_weight": "5 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wtnhbRHwy5uL9u2KU",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "thr"
					},
					"reach": "1,2",
					"parry": "-1",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Thrust",
					"usage_notes": "A hit against a machine target (vehicle, servitor, robot, cyborg limb, or a powered-armour suit's servo/sensor systems) forces that target's HT roll at -3 to avoid a short-circuit, exactly as the Adeptus Mechanicus Arc Pistol's surge effect, regardless of whether the raw damage penetrated DR.\n",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
