		{
			"id": "ege0vRtvNPs2XVwcl",
			"description": "Taser Lance",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A lance-length taser weapon mounted on Skitarii Dragoon walker chassis, current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background depicting a Dragoon's charge as smashing infantry aside with a paralysing jolt rather than a piercing thrust - the walker's own momentum, not the weapon's own field, supplying most of the damage.\n\nDesign: Built on the Imperium Power Lance's own mounted-charge/braced structure (a plain cavalry-lance baseline that gets extra reach and damage only while the mount is moving) but without that entry's power-field bonus, since a taser lance is explicitly an electro-stun weapon, not a disruption-field one: the charge bonus is the mundane momentum bonus alone (thr+2 cr charging, thr+1 cr braced) plus the same HT-3 stun effect as the Taser Goad, reflecting a weapon whose real threat is a walker-speed collision punctuated by a paralysing shock, not a blade that shears through armour. TL11/LC1 (Skitarii walker wargear, one step more restricted than the goads' enforcement-tier LC2).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "3500",
			"base_weight": "12 lb",
