		{
			"id": "eaQUeQQ_u10-cvJjT",
			"description": "Transonic Razor",
			"local_notes": "The transonic field is a toggle (free action), exactly as an Imperial power weapon's disruption field; a depleted or damaged power cell disables it the same way.\n\nLore: The signature weapon of the Sicarian Ruststalker: a blade vibrating at a resonant frequency current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background describes as letting it part armour plate almost without resistance, distinct in the fiction from an Astartes or Militarum disruption-field weapon's shearing, disintegrating bite.\n\nDesign: Deliberately not built as another disruption-field weapon under framework.md's power-field rule (Armor Divisor (10)): the lore describes a mechanically different effect - a resonant vibration that shears through matter cleanly along its own weak points, rather than a field that disrupts molecular bonds outright - so this project gives transonic weapons their own, lesser armour divisor (5) rather than reusing the power-field number wholesale, exactly the kind of \"own derivation, not a renamed catalogue entry\" step framework.md's goals call for. The mundane baseline (sw+1 cut, field off) matches the Power Sword's own one-handed-blade baseline, since underneath the resonant emitter this is still an ordinary well-made blade; the field itself adds +2d+1 rather than the Power Sword's +3d+1, one step down, reflecting a genuinely different (and, per Mechanicus doctrine, less spiritually significant) technology rather than a cut-rate power sword. Checked by exact dice distribution at a representative Sicarian Ruststalker ST of 13 (a cybernetically reinforced combat chassis, sw=2d, giving a field-on total of 4d+1(5), avg 15): it penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 14) 55.6% of the time - a genuine, if no longer overwhelming, threat to rigid infantry plate under the heavier post-rescale carapace DR, still meaningfully \"parting armour\" more often than not - but only 5.4% of the time against Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 20) and effectively never against Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 40), keeping it a devastating anti-infantry weapon without quietly becoming an Astartes-killer, which no depiction supports. TL11 (advanced but not archeotech - Ruststalkers are current-production Cult Mechanicus wargear) and LC0 (Sicarian-pattern kit, chapter-restricted per the Phosphor Serpenta's own LC0 reasoning).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
