		{
			"id": "e0blrFM6g2fELvGdC",
			"description": "Transonic Blades",
			"local_notes": "One blade worn per hand, mirroring the Imperium Lightning Claws' pairing convention: a Ruststalker trained in two-weapon fighting attacks with both under the standard Basic Set dual-weapon rules, with no bespoke \"paired blades\" mechanic added on top.\n\nLore: The alternative Ruststalker loadout to a razor-and-chordclaw pairing: two shorter transonic blades worn as a matched set, background depicting Ruststalkers so equipped as trading the razor's single heavier cut for a faster flurry from both hands, in keeping with their role as an ambush unit that overwhelms a position in a single, brief melee before withdrawing.\n\nDesign: Built the same way the Imperium Lightning Claw is built relative to the Power Sword: a shorter-reach, paired weapon with a smaller field bonus than the family's main blade, applying the Transonic Razor's own +2d+1(5)-over-mundane-baseline logic to a lighter starting weapon (sw-1 cut, one step below the Razor's sw+1, reflecting a shorter blade meant to be worn in pairs) for a total +1d+3 field-on bonus over that baseline (5) armour divisor, unchanged from the Razor's since it's the same underlying resonant technology at a smaller scale. Checked by exact dice distribution at the same representative Ruststalker ST 13 (sw=2d, giving 3d+3(5), avg 13.5): 37.5% against carapace (DR 70, eff. 14), 0.5% against Astartes power armour - a real step below the single Razor's own figures at each tier, matching \"trades the razor's single heavier cut for a faster flurry\" rather than simply doubling its damage output, which this project's Basic Set two-weapon-fighting rules already handle for the \"flurry\" part without a new mechanic. TL11/LC0 as the Transonic Razor.",
