		{
			"id": "eyD5VRa12ZfgpZE9p",
			"description": "Chordclaw",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Sicarian Ruststalker's off-hand weapon, a piston-driven claw on a retractable cable used to snag, entangle and drag a target off-balance or into range of the Ruststalker's transonic blade, background material consistently depicting it as a grip-and-control tool rather than a killing weapon in its own right.\n\nDesign: Built entirely from GURPS's own existing Grapple/Committed Attack rules (B370, B378) rather than a bespoke \"entangle\" mechanic, since GURPS already has exactly the tool this weapon's lore calls for: a low, deliberately unthreatening raw-damage baseline (thr-1 cr, avg 3.5 at a Sicarian ST 9-13 range, never intended to beat any meaningful DR on its own) paired with an automatic grapple attempt on any hit, reflecting a weapon whose entire purpose is to open a target up for the transonic blade rather than to hurt them directly. TL11/LC0 as the rest of the Sicarian Ruststalker's kit.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "4000",
			"base_weight": "6 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wXusxcetwZlRMQYiL",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "thr",
						"base": "-1"
					},
					"reach": "1,2*",
					"parry": "0",
					"strength": "9",
					"usage": "Grapple strike",
					"usage_notes": "A hit (whether or not it does enough damage to matter) lets the wielder immediately attempt a Grapple (B370) as a free follow-up, using this weapon's own skill roll in place of DX for the Quick Contest against the target's ST or DX (target's choice); a target successfully grappled this way suffers the normal -4 to active defenses and must win a Committed Attack (Strong) or an ST-based Escape roll to break free (B378), exactly as an ordinary GURPS grapple. The claw's own reach (marked *) extends to 2 yards only while reeling a grappled target in or holding them at range on the cable; once closed to grip range, treat reach as C for the purposes of the hold.\n",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Spear"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Polearm"
							},
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Staff"
							},
							"modifier": -2
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eW7vCMN-O-nFxF2q-",
			"description": "Arc Maul",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier arc weapon built as a maul rather than a goad or pistol, issued to Skitarii heavy support elements and Mechanicus explorator security teams for close-range work against war machines, cortex-hubs and powered armour rather than infantry - background treats it as a genuine melee weapon rather than the goads' disciplinary tool, but still built around the same \"weak against flesh, strong against machines\" principle as every other arc weapon.\n\nDesign: One step heavier than the Imperium Power Maul's own mundane baseline (sw+2 cr): a built-in coil housing adds enough head mass to justify sw+3 cr even with the field-generation hardware doing none of the cutting, since (per the Arc Pistol/Rifle's own design note) this project does not model the arc-weapon surge as bonus raw damage. The HT-3 surge penalty sits at the goad-and-pistol tier of the family's escalating scale (pistol -2, this maul and the arc goad -3, rifle -4, heavy rifle -6), reflecting a hand weapon's single heavy hit rather than a sustained rifle discharge. Checked by exact dice distribution at a representative Skitarii ST of 12 (sw=2d-1, giving 2d+2, avg 9): 0% penetration against even flak (DR 30) - no real threat to flesh at all, exactly the \"weak against flesh\" half of the family anchor, with its actual combat value entirely in the surge effect against machines. TL11/LC1 (Skitarii combat-issue, one step more restricted than the enforcement-tier goads' LC2).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "2200",
			"base_weight": "6 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wyqKdVJ7NM92RjQqK",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "3"
					},
					"reach": "1",
					"parry": "0",
					"strength": "9",
					"usage": "Swing",
					"usage_notes": "As the Arc Pistol's surge note: a hit against a machine target (vehicle, servitor, robot, cyborg limb, or powered-armour system) forces that target's HT roll at -3 to avoid a short-circuit, regardless of whether the raw damage penetrated DR.\n",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
