				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eF-yi12FWaYfDXL_B",
			"description": "Electroleech Stave",
			"local_notes": "This is the carried stave; the Electro-Priest's Electroleech Staff trait (Fulgurite Pattern, Augmetics file) is the body-integrated FP-drain ability. A Fulgurite who carries this stave gets its crushing swing and stun from the gear and the FP leech from the trait; do not add the trait's damage on top of this stave's damage on the same blow. This entry covers only the physical stave and its built-in electro-stun charge. Current background credits a Fulgurite Electro-Priest's own bio-electric implants (the \"Flesh is Weak\" doctrine and its associated grafts) with letting a charged Electro-Priest turn a hit from this weapon into something far more lethal than the stave's own listed damage - that capability is a character-level trait, not a property of the stave itself, and belongs in a traits file rather than here, per the same separation of concerns this project already applies to the Storm Shield's force-field component and the Blessed Blade's consecration.\n\nLore: The Fulgurite Electro-Priest's iconic weapon: a metal-shod stave built to conduct and discharge massive current into whatever it strikes, current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background describing Electro-Priests as capable of frying a target to component ash when fully charged - a reputation this project attributes chiefly to the Electro-Priest's own bio-electric physiology rather than to the stave as a mundane object.\n\nDesign: Built on the Imperium Power Stave/Shock Staff's own quarterstaff baseline (sw+2 cr/thr+2 cr, reach 1,2) with the electro-stun note bumped one step past the Shock Staff's own HT-3 to HT-4, reflecting a purpose-built high-current weapon rather than a simple riot tool - but deliberately not given the Power Stave's disruption-field damage bonus, since nothing in the lore suggests the stave itself is a power weapon in the framework.md sense; the devastating \"fries a man to ash\" reputation instead belongs, as the notes above explain, to the Electro-Priest's own trait-level physiology (the \"Flesh is Weak\" implants), keeping this equipment entry an honestly modest metal stave with a strong stun charge, the same way the Storm Shield's physical component is \"just\" a very large plate until its trait-level force field is added on top. TL11 for the charge cell; LC1 (Cult Mechanicus cultist-tier wargear, one step more restricted than the general-issue goads).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1800",
