		{
			"id": "emHSX2cjKCHpblRCv",
			"description": "Hydraulic Claw",
			"local_notes": "Slow and clumsy in a defensive sense, as the Imperium Power Fist: cannot be used to Feint, and the -2 parry reflects the actuator's poor reaction speed compared to a natural limb.\n\nLore: A heavy mechanical grasping claw built for prying open bulkheads and hauling wreckage, carried by some Skitarii and Mechanicus combat-menials as an improvised or secondary crushing weapon when a proper melee weapon isn't at hand; background material is consistent that it is fundamentally an industrial tool pressed into service rather than a dedicated war-weapon.\n\nDesign: Deliberately not built on the power-field rule or given any armour divisor at all, unlike the Power Fist it superficially resembles: the Power Fist's whole design note explains that its Armor Divisor (10) comes from an internal disruption field, and nothing in the hydraulic claw's lore or name suggests one - this is pure mechanical leverage, hydraulics compressing rather than a field disrupting, so it stays a flat thr+3d cr with no divisor, following the same \"own derivation, not a renamed catalogue entry\" principle the Power Fist's own design note sets out. Checked by exact dice distribution at a representative Skitarii/Sicarian ST of 14 (thr=1d+2, giving 4d+2 cr, avg 16): it crushes an unarmoured target outright but 0% of hits get through even flak (DR 30) under the current, much heavier post-rescale flak anchor, let alone carapace (DR 70) - a real threat only to unarmoured infantry and light material (matching its lore role prying open bulkheads), exactly what \"an industrial tool, not a war weapon\" should mean mechanically. TL11/LC1.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "3500",
			"base_weight": "25 lb",
