				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eIti12UNmgbkQNiP0",
			"description": "Servo-arm",
			"local_notes": "This is the carried or harness-mounted tool version; the body-grafted implant is the Servo-Arm trait (Adeptus Mechanicus/Traits/Augmetics), which carries its own Lifting and Striking ST. Do not buy both for the same limb. Primarily a repair and maintenance tool (its actual function - fine manipulation, welding and heavy lifting for field repairs - is gear, not a weapon, and belongs in a Mechanicus gear file rather than here); this entry covers only its use as an improvised crushing weapon in a pinch, the way the Imperium Entrenching Tool is priced and statted as a weapon despite being a digging implement first.\n\nLore: Every Tech-Priest's servo-arm - the heavy mechanical limb mounted over one shoulder for repair work - is occasionally shown in Black Library fiction and Codex background swatting an attacker aside or crushing a skull when a Tech-Priest is caught without a proper weapon, always framed as an improvised, clumsy use of a tool built for an entirely different purpose.\n\nDesign: Follows the Imperium Entrenching Tool's own precedent exactly: a mundane tool that is \"already priced and statted as [a weapon], no further penalty needed when used as intended,\" at a correspondingly heavy -3 parry (worse than the Power Fist's -2, since the arm is built for delicate manipulation and heavy static lifting, not for reacting quickly in a fight) and reach C,1 for its long but slow reach. The listed thr+2 cr and ST 10 describe the servo-motor's own modest crushing assist over an unaugmented Tech-Priest's own thrust, not a combat-grade actuator - this is not the Power Fist's disruption-field gauntlet, and does not pretend to threaten anything beyond an unarmoured target. TL11 for the servo-motor itself; LC2 since it is general Mechanicus tech-adept gear rather than Skitarii combat-issue.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "2200",
