			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eakadOiAM_BmpNy1m",
			"description": "Mechadendrite, Combat Tip",
			"local_notes": "This entry is the weapon fitting only - a hardened, piston-driven puncturing spike or hooked blade swapped onto a mechadendrite's mount. The mechadendrite limb itself (an Extra Arm with appropriate reach/DX limitations) is a trait, not equipment, and is defined in a traits file by the traits agent, not here; this item exists so that file's Extra Arms trait has a concrete weapon profile to plug into when a Tech-Priest chooses a combat tip over a manipulator claw or tool interface.\n\nLore: Many Tech-Priests carry one mechadendrite fitted with a combat-capable tip rather than a purely utilitarian manipulator or tool head, background material depicting this as an option chosen by Tech-Priests who expect to see combat (Enginseers and Secutors especially) rather than as universal Mechanicus practice.\n\nDesign: A light, awkward weapon by design: reach C,1 and a poor -2 parry reflect a limb built primarily for fine manipulation rather than combat, with min ST 8 and thr+1 imp describing only the piston-driven spike's own bite, not any augmentation of the wielder's own body (that augmentation, if any, lives in the Extra Arms trait's own ST value, not here). No armour divisor or power field: this is a mundane hardened spike, one clear step below any of the dedicated melee weapons in this file, existing to give a baseline \"what does a combat mechadendrite actually do in a fight\" answer rather than to be anyone's primary weapon. TL11/LC1.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1200",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
