		{
			"id": "eRKANoR5z43fYk8Pr",
			"description": "Kataphron Arc Claw",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The integral close-combat claw of the Kataphron Destroyer and Breacher war-forms, current Codex Adeptus Mechanicus background describing it crushing infantry and light structures alike while its built-in arc discharge shorts out anything electronic it grips - combining raw hydraulic force with the same anti-machine principle as the Mechanicus's smaller arc weapons.\n\nDesign: Combines the Hydraulic Claw's mundane, no-divisor crushing design (a huge hydraulic ram, not a disruption field, per that entry's own reasoning) with the Arc Maul's machine-disabling surge effect at the top of the family's escalating HT-penalty scale (-6, matching the Heavy Arc Rifle's own largest jolt), since a chassis this size carries a proportionally larger capacitor. Checked by exact dice distribution at the Kataphron chassis's own ST of 20 (thr=2d, giving 8d cr, avg 28): it crushes an unarmoured target outright and still gets through flak (DR 30, eff. 30) 30.5% of the time - a real threat even under the heavier post-rescale flak anchor, reflecting the sheer mass behind a Kataphron-scale blow - but, matching the Hydraulic Claw's own reasoning, 0% of hits get through carapace (DR 70) or better with no armour divisor applied - the claw's real threat to anything well-armoured or mechanical is the surge effect, not its raw crushing force, keeping the Kataphron's actual anti-vehicle work with its ranged weapons (the Heavy Grav-cannon and Eradication Ray in the ranged weapons file) rather than this claw, exactly as current Codex background depicts a Kataphron's loadout. TL12 (a purpose-built cybernetic war-form component, not general Skitarii issue) and LC0 (Kataphron husks are Cult Mechanicus-restricted war material in their own right).",
